<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernst Bogislaw von Croÿ</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1620–1684</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ernst Bogislaw of Croÿ</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernst Bogislaw von Croÿ was a grandson of Duke Bogislaw XIII of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> and the last Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamien-pomorski">Cammin</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> assigned the see to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, he handed it over, and in 1650 it became the secular Principality of Cammin. He then served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-elector-of-brandenburg">the Great Elector</a> as governor of Brandenburg Pomerania and later of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Ducal Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernst-bogislaw-von-croy.jpg" alt="Ernst Bogislaw von Croÿ" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Künstler unbekannt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BildErnstBogislawvonCroy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
